                <pb facs="0480" n="400" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg400"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">863.51 Relief Credits/229: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Ives</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-05-15T16:00:00+01:00">May 15, 1930—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 15—2:11 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>25. Department’s 93, April 15, 6 p.m., to the Embassy, Paris [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">London</hi>], I am in receipt of a note, dated May 14th,
                    signed by Minister of Foreign Affairs, wherein it is stated that Denmark, by the
                    declaration made on April 16, last, by the Chairman of the International Relief
                    Bond Committee, has renounced its liens upon the revenues of the Austrian
                    Government derived from customs and tobacco monopoly, on the condition that the
                    Hague agreement of January 20, 1930, come into force and that a similar
                    renunciation is made by the United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ives</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
